WEBVTT

00:00:04.254 --> 00:00:06.340
One, two! One, two, three!

00:00:46.588 --> 00:00:48.549
I've never seen a supernova blow up.

00:00:48.674 --> 00:00:50.676
But if it's anything
like my old Chevy Nova,

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:52.970
- it'll light up the night sky.
- Yeah!

00:00:53.095 --> 00:00:56.306
Anyone who misses this will
regret it the rest of his life.

00:00:56.431 --> 00:01:00.185
- Hey, Fry, could you go make some popcorn?
- Okay.

00:01:04.314 --> 00:01:08.443
Let's go, microwave.
I'm in a hurry here. Hmm?

00:01:19.037 --> 00:01:22.291
Hey.
What smells like blue?

00:01:22.374 --> 00:01:26.461
- Fry, get up here! It's starting!
- Focus!

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:53.071
Hey, which crazy thing happening
are you guys screaming about?

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.277
Ooh! My popcorn's done.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:36.114
Aw. It's less popped than ever.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:39.117
I don't know what happened,
but we've taken on a lot of clocks.

00:02:39.243 --> 00:02:41.119
Let's get back home.

00:02:43.789 --> 00:02:46.250
Why is there so little traffic
around Earth?

00:02:46.375 --> 00:02:48.585
And what's this layer of ozone?

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:50.587
That's never been there before.

00:02:50.712 --> 00:02:52.673
Hmm?

00:02:52.798 --> 00:02:55.092
- Such noises!
- Oh, no!

00:02:55.217 --> 00:02:58.428
There's no global positioning signal.
Navigation is failing!

00:02:58.554 --> 00:03:01.223
- We're gonna crash!
- Not if I can help it.

00:03:01.348 --> 00:03:03.851
Oh. I guess I can't.

00:03:03.976 --> 00:03:06.228
Everyone, put on your seat belts.

00:03:07.312 --> 00:03:10.190
Ah, those things cost
more lives than they save.

00:03:22.411 --> 00:03:26.248
- Bender, are you okay?
- I don't know. I'll try to move my feet.

00:03:29.293 --> 00:03:30.794
All right, here's the plan.

00:03:30.878 --> 00:03:34.923
Zoidberg, pick up the pieces.
Everyone else, take five.

00:03:46.476 --> 00:03:48.562
And Zoidberg picks up another piece!

00:03:48.687 --> 00:03:51.148
The crowd goes wild!

00:03:56.403 --> 00:03:58.030
What is?

00:04:02.201 --> 00:04:06.747
General, in all my years of coverin'
top secret discoveries with sheets,

00:04:06.872 --> 00:04:10.918
I've never dramatically
revealed anything as shocking as this.

00:04:13.462 --> 00:04:16.381
The debris from an alien spaceship.

00:04:18.467 --> 00:04:22.137
Son, I think I can safely say...

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:28.310
As you can see, 1947 is going to be
an eventful year for the town of

00:04:28.435 --> 00:04:31.021
Roswell, New Mexico.

00:04:42.741 --> 00:04:44.618
Remarkable!

00:04:44.743 --> 00:04:47.955
According to the high-precision
digital chronograph

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.749
it's July 9, 1947,

00:04:50.874 --> 00:04:53.627
which would explain why
the chronograph has turned into...

00:04:53.752 --> 00:04:56.380
- this pinup calendar.
- Wait a second.

00:04:56.505 --> 00:04:58.173
You mean we traveled through time?

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:02.094
Doy! Some idiot must have
put metal in the microwave.

00:05:02.219 --> 00:05:04.555
- Yo.
- And the microwave radiation

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:08.725
combined with the gravitons and graviolis
from the supernova,

00:05:08.851 --> 00:05:11.395
blasted us through time itself.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.397
Have you seen today's news?

00:05:13.522 --> 00:05:15.816
"High School Gym Renovations
On Schedule"?

00:05:15.941 --> 00:05:18.443
- What a load!
- No. Over here.

00:05:18.569 --> 00:05:20.612
"Flying Saucer Captured."

00:05:20.737 --> 00:05:22.739
That's no flying saucer.

00:05:22.865 --> 00:05:25.409
- That's my ass!
- My God!

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:29.788
This means the flying saucer
that crashed in Roswell was us!

00:05:29.913 --> 00:05:33.500
And the alien they captured
was... was...

00:05:35.586 --> 00:05:37.462
- Hello.
- Ewww!

00:05:37.588 --> 00:05:42.009
So what are you guys doing tonight?
I'm up for whatever.

00:05:46.388 --> 00:05:48.557
Yes. We tore the universe a new

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.685
space-hole all right,
but it's clenching shut fast.

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:54.229
Our only hope to get back
to our own time

00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:56.481
is to go back through it
within, oh, say

00:05:56.607 --> 00:06:00.402
exactly 24 hours.

00:06:00.527 --> 00:06:02.362
No problem.

00:06:02.487 --> 00:06:04.281
The ship's fixed
except for the cup holder,

00:06:04.364 --> 00:06:06.408
and I should have that
operational within 10 hours.

00:06:06.533 --> 00:06:10.454
You've got eight. But a more
urgent concern is the microwave.

00:06:10.579 --> 00:06:14.458
Without a working one, we have no hope
of returning to the future.

00:06:14.583 --> 00:06:17.920
Well, I'm sure we can buy a microwave
somewhere around here.

00:06:18.045 --> 00:06:21.590
Meanwhile, you guys sneak onto the army
base and rescue Bender's body.

00:06:21.715 --> 00:06:25.052
Hey, and while we're on the base,
I'll visit my Grandfather Enos.

00:06:25.177 --> 00:06:28.138
- He was stationed at Roswell.
- Your grandfather?

00:06:28.263 --> 00:06:30.724
Stay away from him,
you dimwitted monkey!

00:06:30.849 --> 00:06:32.726
You mustn't interfere
with the past.

00:06:32.851 --> 00:06:35.354
Don't do anything
that affects anything

00:06:35.479 --> 00:06:37.606
unless it turns out
you were supposed to do it,

00:06:37.731 --> 00:06:41.443
in which case, for the love of God,
don't not do it!

00:06:41.568 --> 00:06:42.653
Got it.

00:06:42.736 --> 00:06:45.030
If, for example, you were
to kill your grandfather,

00:06:45.155 --> 00:06:46.949
you'd cease to exist.

00:06:47.074 --> 00:06:50.035
But existing is basically all I do!

00:06:53.539 --> 00:06:56.416
- What is your purpose here?
- Huh?

00:06:56.542 --> 00:06:58.919
All right, Officer.
I'll move along.

00:06:59.044 --> 00:07:02.089
What the general means is
why did you come to Earth?

00:07:02.214 --> 00:07:05.717
Not a day goes by
I don't ask myself the same question.

00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:31.910
Enos!

00:07:34.121 --> 00:07:37.249
Private, I want that toilet bowl so clean,
I could eat off it!

00:07:37.332 --> 00:07:40.961
- 'Cause I intend to!
- Well, gadzooks, Sarge.

00:07:41.086 --> 00:07:43.505
It's him!
It's my Grandfather Enos!

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:47.718
Now prepare my lunch
and place it in the latrine at 1200 hours!

00:07:53.515 --> 00:07:56.768
That jeep's gonna hit him,
and I won't exist anymore!

00:07:59.021 --> 00:08:01.190
Hey!

00:08:03.233 --> 00:08:06.570
Are you crazy?
You almost got yourself run over.

00:08:06.695 --> 00:08:09.156
I did?
Then I sure am lucky you knocked me

00:08:09.281 --> 00:08:11.533
onto this pile of rusty bayonets.

00:08:11.658 --> 00:08:14.411
Psst! Fry,
stop interfering with history!

00:08:14.536 --> 00:08:17.581
I don't want to have to memorize
a lot of new kings when I get back.

00:08:17.706 --> 00:08:19.917
I had no choice.
I was about to not exist.

00:08:20.042 --> 00:08:22.920
I could feel myself fading away,
like Greg Kinnear.

00:08:24.087 --> 00:08:27.299
Well, thanks, soldier.
I'm off to make Sarge's lunch.

00:08:27.382 --> 00:08:30.052
Handlin' raw chicken?
Best part of the job.

00:08:30.344 --> 00:08:33.347
Mmm! Finger-lickin' good.

00:08:33.472 --> 00:08:36.934
That's it! This place is too dangerous.
We gotta get you out of here.

00:08:37.059 --> 00:08:38.769
Everything's gonna be
all right, Dad.

00:08:38.894 --> 00:08:41.563
Well, gadzooks!
I'd better ask Sarge.

00:08:41.688 --> 00:08:43.732
No time! Run!
Run to safety!

00:08:53.659 --> 00:08:57.246
This experiment will determine
what food, if any,

00:08:57.329 --> 00:08:59.331
the alien eats.

00:09:05.045 --> 00:09:09.258
A buffet! Oh, if only I had
my wallet with me.

00:09:09.383 --> 00:09:11.552
Um, it's free.

00:09:21.979 --> 00:09:24.189
Get me the president.

00:09:30.362 --> 00:09:32.781
Fry's from around this time.
I'll talk like him.

00:09:32.906 --> 00:09:35.784
Yo, homes!
We're looking for a microwave oven.

00:09:35.909 --> 00:09:38.203
Microwave? Never heard
of that brand, sweetheart.

00:09:38.328 --> 00:09:40.289
What you want is
the deluxe gas princess.

00:09:40.414 --> 00:09:43.041
This beauty has four broilers,
a casserole indicator,

00:09:43.166 --> 00:09:46.628
a fold-out ironing board,
and down here a foot-soaking tub

00:09:46.753 --> 00:09:49.840
since, as a woman,
you'll be standing in front of it all day.

00:09:51.884 --> 00:09:53.510
Oh. I'm sorry.

00:09:53.635 --> 00:09:58.056
Now, I'll "ax" you again.
Where can we find a microwave?

00:09:58.182 --> 00:10:00.809
Sir, your wife's hysterical,
so I'll address this to you.

00:10:00.934 --> 00:10:03.896
This oven is lightning fast.
It takes only five hours to cook a roast.

00:10:04.021 --> 00:10:05.898
Ooh! That's good news.

00:10:06.023 --> 00:10:09.693
You know, you really don't cook
enough roasts, Leela.

00:10:11.069 --> 00:10:12.946
Ohh. Women!

00:10:18.035 --> 00:10:21.496
Oh! Thank God I got you off
that dangerous army base.

00:10:21.622 --> 00:10:23.665
You sure are
the helpful type, stranger.

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:27.169
Say, you got anything to eat
in that there lunch box?

00:10:27.294 --> 00:10:30.881
- What...
- Ooh. Snacks.

00:10:31.006 --> 00:10:35.302
Hey, that's my brain!

00:10:35.427 --> 00:10:38.722
Man. Them crackers
cut my mouth up somethin' bad.

00:10:38.847 --> 00:10:40.724
Let's stop off for a malt.

00:10:47.856 --> 00:10:51.777
- See that waitress there?
- Yowzah! I know what I want for dessert.

00:10:51.902 --> 00:10:53.820
That's my fiancée, Mildred.

00:10:53.946 --> 00:10:56.615
Grandma Mildred?
Uh, no dessert. Just coffee.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:59.284
Okey-doke.
And for you, snuggums?

00:10:59.409 --> 00:11:03.080
Uh, I'll have a pie
with a fried egg on top.

00:11:05.332 --> 00:11:06.667
Yeah, she sure is pretty.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:09.169
You ought to marry her and father
some children right away.

00:11:09.294 --> 00:11:12.214
Yeah, folks say that.
But did you ever get the feeling

00:11:12.339 --> 00:11:15.384
you're only goin' with girls
'cause you're supposed to?

00:11:15.509 --> 00:11:17.302
What?

00:11:17.427 --> 00:11:20.097
Don't ever, ever say
or think that again!

00:11:20.222 --> 00:11:22.182
Please, just concentrate
on staying alive.

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:25.435
Fire! Look out!

00:11:27.521 --> 00:11:29.690
You almost got neutered.

00:11:29.815 --> 00:11:32.025
Well, 'taint as bad as gettin' killed.

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:35.696
For me it is!
I'm getting you out of here.

00:11:35.821 --> 00:11:39.366
Ow!

00:11:46.456 --> 00:11:50.043
Okay, we're in the middle of nowhere,
which is the safest part of nowhere.

00:11:50.169 --> 00:11:52.963
Just stay put
and enjoy this calendar.

00:12:03.974 --> 00:12:08.187
Safe and sound. Finally,
I can continue to exist.

00:12:14.234 --> 00:12:17.029
Three, two, one.

00:12:34.421 --> 00:12:39.134
And you are outta here!

00:12:46.099 --> 00:12:49.311
- What'll you folks have today?
- I'll have the soylent green

00:12:49.436 --> 00:12:53.482
with a slice of soylent orange
and some soylent coleslaw.

00:12:53.607 --> 00:12:56.485
- Pardon?
- It's the 20th century, Professor.

00:12:56.610 --> 00:12:59.905
Oh, right. I'll have
a croque monsieur,

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:03.534
the paella, two mutton pills
and a stein of mead.

00:13:03.659 --> 00:13:05.744
I'll just have a small injection
of Fem-a-slim.

00:13:05.869 --> 00:13:08.622
Uh, two chili dogs
comin' up.

00:13:08.747 --> 00:13:12.626
Well, settle in. Without a microwave,
we're trapped in this time period.

00:13:12.751 --> 00:13:14.628
Oh, Lord!

00:13:14.753 --> 00:13:17.673
We'll have to endure
the horrible music of the Big Bopper,

00:13:17.798 --> 00:13:20.259
and then the terrible
tragedy of his death.

00:13:21.718 --> 00:13:25.556
Wait a second! There's a microwave
radar dish at the army base.

00:13:25.681 --> 00:13:28.559
- We could steal it.
- No! That would alter history.

00:13:28.684 --> 00:13:34.022
Above all else, it is our sacred duty
to preserve the past exactly as it was.

00:13:34.147 --> 00:13:36.859
- Well, I killed my grandfather.
- Wha...

00:13:36.984 --> 00:13:40.279
Wait. If you killed your grandfather,
why do you still exist?

00:13:40.404 --> 00:13:42.281
I don't know.
Maybe God loves me.

00:13:42.406 --> 00:13:45.659
Oh!

00:13:45.784 --> 00:13:48.829
Killed? In an atomic blast?

00:13:48.954 --> 00:13:51.874
No, sir. I'm afraid
I don't take much solace in the fact

00:13:51.957 --> 00:13:54.793
that the implosion trigger
functioned perfectly.

00:13:54.918 --> 00:13:57.254
Ah.

00:13:57.379 --> 00:14:01.300
There, there. If it makes you feel any
better, his body was vaporized,

00:14:01.425 --> 00:14:03.844
so there's no chance of him
coming back as a zombie.

00:14:03.969 --> 00:14:07.764
- I'm not worried about that.
- Then you're a braver woman than I.

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:12.019
You remind me of Enos.
Would you mind walking me home?

00:14:12.144 --> 00:14:13.687
How far is it?

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:31.830
Welcome to Roswell,
President Truman.

00:14:31.955 --> 00:14:35.042
Fellas, this visit's top secret.
No one's to know about it...

00:14:35.167 --> 00:14:37.044
except the senior officers, scientists,

00:14:37.169 --> 00:14:39.129
and a single conspiracy nut
who no one will believe.

00:14:49.431 --> 00:14:52.601
Mr. President, our experts
have reassembled the parts

00:14:52.726 --> 00:14:55.646
from the alien ship
into its original design.

00:14:56.772 --> 00:14:59.149
Hmm.

00:14:59.274 --> 00:15:03.237
Whistlin' Dixie!
I want this sent to Area 51 for study.

00:15:03.362 --> 00:15:06.240
But, sir, that's where
we're building the fake moon landing set.

00:15:06.365 --> 00:15:08.200
Then we'll have to
really land on the moon.

00:15:08.325 --> 00:15:11.203
Invent NASA and tell them
to get off their fannies!

00:15:11.328 --> 00:15:14.665
If you come in peace,
surrender or be destroyed.

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:16.667
If you're here to make war,
we surrender.

00:15:16.792 --> 00:15:20.546
Both good. The important thing is
I'm meeting new people.

00:15:20.671 --> 00:15:22.631
Bushwah! Now, what's your mission?

00:15:22.756 --> 00:15:25.217
Are you planning to make
some kind of alien-human hybrid?

00:15:25.342 --> 00:15:29.179
- Are you coming on to me?
- Hot crackers! I take exception to that!

00:15:29.304 --> 00:15:31.223
I'm not hearing a "no."

00:15:31.348 --> 00:15:33.976
Nerts to this space crab!
If we want information,

00:15:34.101 --> 00:15:36.436
we'll have to do us
an old-fashioned alien autopsy.

00:15:37.479 --> 00:15:39.273
Hooray!

00:15:45.612 --> 00:15:49.199
Every little thing
reminds me of Enos.

00:15:51.076 --> 00:15:53.829
Aw. I know how you feel.

00:15:53.954 --> 00:15:56.248
My grandfather died recently.

00:15:58.250 --> 00:16:00.836
It's all so sad.

00:16:00.961 --> 00:16:05.215
At times like this,
I just need someone to hold me.

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:09.011
Mmm.
You like holdin' me, don't you?

00:16:09.136 --> 00:16:11.054
Hey, you know what
always cheers you up?

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:13.307
Baking me a nice tray
of sugar cookies.

00:16:13.432 --> 00:16:16.018
How about these cookies, sugar?

00:16:16.143 --> 00:16:18.061
I shouldn't be here.

00:16:18.187 --> 00:16:21.106
I shouldn't even exist.
But I do exist,

00:16:21.231 --> 00:16:24.860
which proves you can't really
be my grandm...

00:16:24.985 --> 00:16:26.945
Mmm!

00:16:42.836 --> 00:16:45.964
Oh, my God!

00:16:46.882 --> 00:16:48.842
Huh?

00:16:50.886 --> 00:16:53.972
- What the hell have you done, Fry?
- Relax.

00:16:54.097 --> 00:16:56.683
She can't be my grandmother.
I figured it all out.

00:16:56.808 --> 00:16:59.937
Of course she's your grandmother,
you perverted dope!

00:17:00.062 --> 00:17:04.358
- Look!
- Come back to bed, dearie.

00:17:04.483 --> 00:17:06.360
It's impossible!

00:17:06.485 --> 00:17:09.488
I mean, if she's my grandmother,
who's my grandfather?

00:17:09.613 --> 00:17:12.324
Isn't it obvious?

00:17:12.449 --> 00:17:16.119
You are.

00:17:19.706 --> 00:17:23.585
Did you say something, dearie?
I'm a bit hard of hearing.

00:17:30.843 --> 00:17:33.595
Commencing excavation
of the subject's chest cavity.

00:17:33.679 --> 00:17:36.640
And in this corner, Zoidberg!

00:17:36.765 --> 00:17:39.601
Come on, lighten up.

00:17:39.726 --> 00:17:42.145
What is this, a funeral?

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:46.316
- Heart.
- Take. I've got four of them.

00:17:46.441 --> 00:17:48.777
one deviled egg.

00:17:48.902 --> 00:17:52.239
Deviled egg?

00:17:52.364 --> 00:17:54.241
The same deviled egg.

00:17:58.829 --> 00:18:01.164
- Snap out of it!
- Start the ship, Leela.

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:05.210
Let's just steal the damn radar dish
and get back to our own time.

00:18:05.335 --> 00:18:07.212
But-But won't that
change history?

00:18:07.337 --> 00:18:10.132
Oh, a lesson in not changing history

00:18:10.257 --> 00:18:12.384
from Mr. "I'm My Own Grandpa."

00:18:12.509 --> 00:18:16.013
Let's get the hell out of here already!
Screw history!

00:18:37.618 --> 00:18:40.162
U.F.O.! U.F.O.!

00:18:45.959 --> 00:18:49.171
Hey, don't cut that.
I need that to speak.

00:18:54.343 --> 00:18:56.220
- Oh, my...
- Great Roosevelt's ghost!

00:19:02.392 --> 00:19:04.478
Take this, Mr. President, sir!

00:19:08.148 --> 00:19:10.692
The president is gagging
on my gas bladder.

00:19:10.776 --> 00:19:12.819
What an honor.

00:19:15.364 --> 00:19:17.282
Wha...

00:19:17.366 --> 00:19:19.618
Oh, right.

00:19:35.884 --> 00:19:39.221
- Enos!
- He's dead! Sorry!

00:20:01.743 --> 00:20:03.954
Choke on that, causality!

00:20:04.079 --> 00:20:08.292
1947 can kiss my shiny metal...

00:20:13.172 --> 00:20:15.299
Turn around!
We've gotta go back for Bender!

00:20:15.424 --> 00:20:19.094
Impossible!
The supernova time hole is closing.

00:20:19.219 --> 00:20:23.265
If we don't leave now,
we'll never get back to the 31st century.

00:20:25.684 --> 00:20:28.979
Whoa!

00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:35.277
Bender!

00:20:46.079 --> 00:20:47.956
There. Good as new.

00:20:48.081 --> 00:20:50.501
- Don't you need this one?
- Oh, no!

00:20:50.626 --> 00:20:53.128
That's my...

00:20:56.924 --> 00:20:59.176
Gotcha.

00:20:59.301 --> 00:21:01.386
Oh. Poor Bender.

00:21:01.512 --> 00:21:04.097
He must be so lonely right now,

00:21:04.223 --> 00:21:06.767
trapped a thousand years in the past.

00:21:06.892 --> 00:21:08.769
Hey, wait a second!

00:21:15.442 --> 00:21:17.319
- Anything?
- No.

00:21:17.444 --> 00:21:19.321
Wait!

00:21:19.446 --> 00:21:21.114
Ow! Stupid jerk!

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:24.034
- He's alive!
- Whee!

00:21:26.578 --> 00:21:30.916
Bender! What was it like lying in
that hole for a thousand years?

00:21:31.041 --> 00:21:33.335
I was enjoying it
until you guys showed up.

00:21:33.460 --> 00:21:36.755
Well, now everything
is back as it was.

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:38.590
And if history doesn't care that our

00:21:38.674 --> 00:21:41.760
degenerate friend Fry
is his own grandfather,

00:21:41.885 --> 00:21:43.762
then who are we to judge?

00:21:43.887 --> 00:21:45.556
Amen!